{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples","id":1449664,"title":"[Aberrant] Understanding Scale through specific examples","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-26T08:56:00-07:00","id":1449664,"title":"[Aberrant] Understanding Scale through specific examples","content":"As I'm familiarizing myself more with Storypath in general and Aberrant in particular, I thought it might be beneficial to have a thread where folks can post examples of their understanding of Scale interactions. I know these have been tricky for people to wrap their head around, myself included, so having some more concrete use cases to discuss could help.<br /> <br /> Let's say we have a nova with Toughness 3, giving them Soft Armor (1) and Scale 3 durability, with Defense 1. For purposes of this example, the nova won't roll a Resilience attribute to defend.<br /> <br /> The example soldier from page 261 of the Aberrant book shoots at the nova. They have a Combat pool of 7, so on average they will roll 2.1 successes; we'll round down to 2. With their Enhancement 1 from their equipment, they have a total of 3 successes.<br /> <br /> They spend 1 success to hit a Defense of 1, leaving 2 successes to purchase Stunts. Normally, they could spend 1 of these to overcome the Soft Armor (1) for Inflict Damage, and the second for Pin Down or something else. However, in this case the nova has Scale 3 durability, against the Scale 2 damage inflicted by the rifle the soldier is using. 1 difference in Scale adds +2 Difficulty, so this would increase the Difficulty of the Inflict Damage stunt to 3, one more success than the soldier has available, so the nova takes the hit with no consequences.<br /> <br /> Is that all accurate? This is based on an average result from the soldier, so if they got lucky and rolled 3+ successes on 7 dice, they could still injure the nova. Then again, the nova would presumably roll for Defensive Stunts, decreasing the number of successes the soldier would have available to purchase Inflict Damage. (Aside: seems odd that you would roll Resilience instead of Finesse for purposes of defense/dodging.)<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any feedback!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/361-brighthand","name":"Brighthand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T09:15:31-07:00","id":1449668,"title":"","content":"Yes, it\u2019s accurate.<br /> <br /> Its not a regular rifle that have Scale 2 damage, usually they are scale 1, but with the Heavy Weapon tag it can be 2. With a regular rifle the soldier would need 5 successes (beside the defense) to cause damage, 1 from soft armor plus 4 from 2 scales above.<br /> <br /> Now, the pin down stunt you suggested, is a bit complex with the scale gap. While it don\u2019t say anything about scale, you would not be able to pin down a virtually bullet proof nova, so I would allow to use this stunt only if you spend 2 extra successes per scale to break the scale difference, but it\u2019s not RAW.<br /> <br /> If you want to improve the soldier chances, you may use the Heavy weapon (you were using before) to increase the savage by 1, and the Two handed tag, that add 1 extra enhancement to damage. The Emptying the Magazine stunt can also be used for extra 2 enhancements, but will force a reload next round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T13:18:42-07:00","id":1449694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1449668#post1449668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it\u2019s accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huzzah! Glad I have understood the basics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1449668#post1449668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not a regular rifle that have Scale 2 damage, usually they are scale 1, but with the Heavy Weapon tag it can be 2. With a regular rifle the soldier would need 5 successes (beside the defense) to cause damage, 1 from soft armor plus 4 from 2 scales above.</div> </div> </div> </div>So even though the example given for Scale 2 power on the chart on page 164 is &quot;pistol, rifle&quot;, they are actually a Scale 1 effect when wielded by a normal person, unless they have the Heavy Weapon tag? Makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1449668#post1449668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the pin down stunt you suggested, is a bit complex with the scale gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was just mentioning that in context of the example, giving them something else to do with the leftover success, but understood and agreed on your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1449668#post1449668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to improve the soldier chances, you may use the Heavy weapon (you were using before) to increase the savage by 1, and the Two handed tag, that add 1 extra enhancement to damage. The Emptying the Magazine stunt can also be used for extra 2 enhancements, but will force a reload next round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's put it all together!<br /> <br /> Nova - Toughness 3, Stamina 3, Defense 1<br /> <br /> Soldier - Combat Pool 7, using a rifle with the Automatic, Heavy Weapon and Two-Handed Qualities (+1 Enhancement, +1 Scale, +1 Enhancement to Inflict Damage).<br /> <br /> The soldier rolls 2 successes on their pool, plus 2 Enhancement from the rifle, one of which must go toward Inflict Damage, for a total of 4 successes. They also use the Emptying the Magazine Stunt, adding 2 more Enhancement, for a total of 6 successes.<br /> <br /> The nova rolls Stamina 3 and gets 1 success, making their Defense 2.<br /> <br /> The soldier spends 2 successes to hit the nova, leaving 4 successes. The Heavy Weapon rifle has Scale 2 power against the nova's Scale 3 durability, increasing the cost of the Inflict Damage stunt from 1 to 3. The soldier spends 3 successes and successfully inflicts a Bruised Injury Condition on the nova. Of course, they now have to reload, and presumably have an irritated superhuman bearing down on them...<br /> <br /> EDIT TO ADD: The Heavy Weapon tag does a lot of...heavy lifting here. Using the standard Assault Rifle from Trinity core, the soldier loses out on +1 Enhancement and +1 Scale. In that scenario, on an average roll of 2 successes, +1 Enhancement to Inflict Damage from Two-Handed and +2 Enhancement from Emptying the Magazine, they're down to 5 successes. Spending 2 to overcome the nova's Defense leaves them with 3. However, since it's now only a Scale 1 attack, their cost to purchase Inflict Damage is 5 successes, so they are out of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/361-brighthand","user":"Brighthand","date":". 05-26-2021, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/361-brighthand","name":"Brighthand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T14:30:46-07:00","id":1449696,"title":"","content":"the \u201cguns are scale 2\u201d thing is a bit confusing, and it shows up in every other book, sometimes it disappear, sometimes don\u2019t (like happened in Aberrant).<br /> <br /> About the Heavy Weapon tag: Exactly! There is another tag that increase scale, but it\u2019s just for Aeon, it\u2019s the Extreme Force tag from Aexpansion. It takes away the issues to move around carrying the weapon, but you must recharge (or it\u2019s a single shot, there are 2 versions of the tag) but in this case you can\u2019t use emptying the magazine stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-26-2021, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T13:12:28-07:00","id":1450345,"title":"","content":"If I'm not mistaken, different weapons can have different scales. The scale sections mention it, as does section determining the number of weapon tags. It is also tangential mentioned in the super science section. Its just missing in the section for building weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T16:14:38-07:00","id":1450516,"title":"","content":"Different weapons can have different scales, but as a general rule, all personal weapons are scale 1 except if have a tag that increases it (like Heavy Weapon, for example).<br /> <br /> The scale granted by super tech is not about damage. Believe me, scale does a big difference in game and having a pistol capable of scale 3 because it\u2019s a inspired item is not nice for Core games or even for Aberrant games, your nova would feel weaker if a pistol can put them down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T04:47:13-07:00","id":1450799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1450516#post1450516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different weapons can have different scales, but as a general rule, all personal weapons are scale 1 except if have a tag that increases it (like Heavy Weapon, for example).<br /> <br /> The scale granted by super tech is not about damage. Believe me, scale does a big difference in game and having a pistol capable of scale 3 because it\u2019s a inspired item is not nice for Core games or even for Aberrant games, your nova would feel weaker if a pistol can put them down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it mention the personal weapons are scale 1? I've not seen that in the core or in aberrant. <br /> <br /> What do you mean its not about damage? I'm confused with what you are saying. If my nova doesnt have any durability or armor, a super tech pistol should put them down, but even that is unlikely with only 4 damage possible. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:46:04-07:00","id":1452203,"title":"","content":"Something that\u2019s just occurred to me, I might be wrong and being a bit bit picky but shouldn\u2019t toughness 3 give you scale 4 durability.<br /> <br /> How I see it:<br /> - you start with scale 1 durability<br /> - toughness 1 counts as wearing armour with soft 1 and complete 3 tags. This to me counts as scale 2 durability.<br /> - 2 more dots to get toughness 3 which gives +2 to durability scale and you get scale 4 durability.<br /> <br /> What does everyone think. It just seems to match the other mega stats and edges which I think max out at scale 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T12:55:32-07:00","id":1452207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This to me counts as scale 2 durability. </div> </div> </div>Technically, it doesn't. I has to state it's a scale increase. Besides, durability scale gives 2 soft armor, not one. So, you get less benefit than durability scale would give you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:09:59-07:00","id":1452210,"title":"","content":"I thought toughness 1 counts as wearing armour soft 1, complete 3. Where does the soft 2 come from?<br /> <br /> If toughness 3 only grants scale 3 durability won\u2019t it always lag behind mega might 3 which grants scale 4 power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:25:33-07:00","id":1452214,"title":"","content":"Excess durability scale gives you +2 soft armor per excess durability scale level against an attack.<br /> <br /> Toughness 3 gives you 1 soft armor +2 durability scale for a total of 3. Yes, mega-might 3 gives you 4 power scale. You're down 1 net success. This is a good thing. You always want attacks to be at least slightly more powerful than defense, because otherwise it makes combats drag on long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T13:52:15-07:00","id":1452224,"title":"","content":"Oh that make sense, I didn\u2019t think if that way. I was only thinking that the mega\u2019s scales weren\u2019t equal and durability wouldn\u2019t reach scale 10. But I suppose you can buy tags to improve toughness and also have access to other mega edges which grant more health levels and defence it all equals out in the end.<br /> <br /> Thanks for explaining that for me it was really confusing me why is was set up like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T18:20:25-07:00","id":1452259,"title":"","content":"One of the things that confuses me is that the description of Mega-Might talks about increasing power scale for damage to objects but not attacks.<br /> For example:<br /> A<br /> character with Might 3 throws a punch against a nova was toughness 3, is this attack scale 1 or 4? Would anything change if the character had the claws body modification?<br /> <br /> A character with mega might 3 makes an attack with an attuned sword against a nova with toughness 3 is this scale 1 (sword) or scale (4 the attack). What about a qtech sword with a +8 enhancement bonus?<br /> <br /> <br /> A character with mega dex 3 make an attack with an attuned sword, again scale 1 or 4.<br /> <br /> A character with mega dex uses a sniper rifle to make an attack, is the scale increased (above that for the weapon)? (Note that if a sword gets a scale increase, you can combine the physical attack cale bonus with a high enhancement qtech item, but can't do the same with a gun).<br /> <br /> A normal human size opponent is almost always size scale 1. Does this mean that you get a different number of enhancement points to using shove/knockdown with might (compare to size) than an attack? (This does seem like comic book combat where somebody can get sent through a wall but suffer only minimum damage). Does this mean that somebody with Mega Might 4 (scale 5) is more than 3 scale factors larger than normal human size, and can send a human size opponent flying at will? If so can a strong/large&amp;strongt enough character launch an opponent into orbit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T19:25:52-07:00","id":1452266,"title":"","content":"Mega Dexterity does not give you Scale. You should re-read Mega-Attributes: they DO NOT work simply by &quot;adding Scale to the Attribute&quot; - the situations that they give Scale are much narrower, and Mega Dex doesn't give you Scale at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T19:36:12-07:00","id":1452268,"title":"","content":"Well I was pretty sure the answer for dex would be no, but for might<br /> <br /> Mega-Might increases a nova\u2019s muscle power far beyond human limits. At high levels, Mega-Might novas can lift multiple tons and smash steel and stone with their bare hands. Like several other nova abilities, MegaMight is at least partially based in a nova\u2019s ability to manipulate quantum forces \u2014 no amount of body modification would allow a human-sized being to exert the kind of force powerful Mega-Might novas do. At least part of their power seems to bend or ignore concepts like leverage or structural weaknesses. Mega-Might novas:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Increase might Scale by their Mega-Might dots<br /> for lifting and moving, and power Scale for<br /> damaging things using sheer muscle power.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The nova can also throw anything they can lift<br /> a number of range bands equal to their MegaMight dots (Extreme range at Mega-Might 4+).<br /> If they throw an object as an attack, it gains the<br /> Thrown and Pushing tags.<br /> <br /> Which still brings up the question of, things as in inanimate objects or things as in everything (I tend to go with the latter). Also is using a sword damage u8sing sheer muscle power (I'd tend to think claws and punching would fall into sheer muscle power). Also it seem like might scale is being increased, which would would oppose size scale for pushing attempts. So it would seem you have a separate set of scale enhancements for damage and knockback.<br /> <br /> Which still doesn't answer the question if I have grow 5 can a finger flick a human size attacker into orbit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T19:52:39-07:00","id":1452270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrSteve</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1452268#post1452268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Increase might Scale by their Mega-Might dots for lifting and moving, and power Scale for damaging things using sheer muscle power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, damage <i>anything </i>that can take physical damage, people included; also for lifting <i>anything </i>(including people). :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T23:05:52-07:00","id":1452281,"title":"","content":"Well I think I've found the answer to the weapons scale argument. Both small arms and Kevlar are scale 2. Shoot somebody without armor, get a scale bump, shoot somebody with armor, things resolve normally. On the other hand Qtech armor is scale 9 and novatech scale 7. That seems a bit much (and there is no rule to buy such armor).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25593-drsteve","name":"DrSteve","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T02:37:21-07:00","id":1452296,"title":"","content":"The increase in scale with bare hand punches is a big question mark to me to, you can have both approaches, and I think it\u2019s a SG option.<br /> Honestly I would make MMight not increase scale of punches, giving you 2 options to do so while fighting, using large objects as weapons (as you can lift them easily) or have a Quantum attack that works as your \u201cbare hand punch\u201d.<br /> This option balance MMight to the other physical MAtts (none giving scale in combat).<br /> That also gives you an explanation of why using cars and posts to hit the enemy is pretty common in comic combats, while punch would have the same result by the rules.<br /> <br /> Now on weapon/armor scale.<br /> You CAN use weapons and armors giving scale as described in the table or can consider them all scale 1 as standard, it\u2019s up to the SG. In Aberrant specifically, we deal with a lot of scale and giving scale to guns would have not that much impact in the game, but in a Core game it would have a lot.<br /> First, it would make guns extremely lethal (like in real life), possibly making any attack against an unarmored target almost a instant take out.<br /> It would make most characters afraid of jumping into gunshots (like in real life), and fights, once you are armed, would be rare and fast.<br /> You would also need to add scale to other big weapons, like swords and axes, as those weapons do as much damage as a gun, but small knives would be still scale 1 weapons.<br /> My approach on this is, ignore the table and follow the rules described in Core, all weapons are scale 1 unless they have tags that increase it.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Qtech and Nova tech weapons and armors use super science rules to be built, and are built using powers and regular tags, so you CAN build an scale 9 armor, but it would be a rank 9 item and you would also need Q9 to use it, something that is not present in Aberrant era (at least not at the standard Aberrant game).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T06:06:11-07:00","id":1452312,"title":"","content":"Q-Tech is +3 scale on what you build. So Q-Tech Kevlar would be scale 5 if kevlar is scale 2. . The Rank doesnt imply scale those are two different measurements. <br /> <br /> Combat is lengthy and it's impossible to one shot kill any PC with a scale 1 or 2 weapon. And if they are combat focused, thats far harder. <br /> <br /> Not to mention cover which has huge health pools. <br /> <br /> Given that, guns should be a scale 2 unless they are like a derringer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T07:23:17-07:00","id":1452323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1452296#post1452296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The increase in scale with bare hand punches is a big question mark to me to, you can have both approaches, and I think it\u2019s a SG option.<br /> Honestly I would make MMight not increase scale of punches, giving you 2 options to do so while fighting, using large objects as weapons (as you can lift them easily) or have a Quantum attack that works as your \u201cbare hand punch\u201d.<br /> <br /> That also gives you an explanation of why using cars and posts to hit the enemy is pretty common in comic combats, while punch would have the same result by the rules.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>So you just dont think people should be able to make the Hulk, Luke Cage, or Superman using Might? People who punch hard? Both options of using Q-Attack and Mega Strength are valid no SG interpretation needed. <br /> <br /> @Dr. Steve<br /> Also, Durability above Power adds to the amount of Success require to do Inflict Injure, but it also adds to Defense. So it helps with knockback too.<br /> Increase in Size scale will generally also increase Might and Durability scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10020,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","user":"Manifoldpersona","date":".  SG not needed. 06-15-2021, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:38:27-07:00","id":1452341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manifoldpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1452323#post1452323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you just dont think people should be able to make the Hulk, Luke Cage, or Superman using Might? People who punch hard? Both options of using Q-Attack and Mega Strength are valid no SG interpretation needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood what I meant. But yes, kind of...<br /> <br /> The idea is, your favorite super strong hero (let\u2019s put him on Scale 3) has a quantum attack that is his punch, basically the power is Q-Attack 3 with the tags Brutal, Pushing and Piercing (that seams a good combination of tags, but you could pick others), no special effects (flash of light, energy, what ever) nor range (melee). Basically a scale 3 punch that cause a lot of damage, send people flying and can ignore armor.<br /> <br /> The bad part is that he needs to spend quantum to gain scale, so he will get tired of punching people around, unless you get a duration tag or a reduced cost tag. But it would leave no question on how to deal with the punch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T09:56:09-07:00","id":1452346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1452341#post1452341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea is, your favorite super strong hero (let\u2019s put him on Scale 3) has a quantum attack that is his punch, basically the power is Q-Attack 3 with the tags Brutal, Pushing and Piercing (that seams a good combination of tags, but you could pick others), no special effects (flash of light, energy, what ever) nor range (melee). Basically a scale 3 punch that cause a lot of damage, send people flying and can ignore armor.<br /> <br /> The bad part is that he needs to spend quantum to gain scale, so he will get tired of punching people around, unless you get a duration tag or a reduced cost tag. But it would leave no question on how to deal with the punch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could easily make a quantum attack punch, and it makes definitely sense for speedsters. And you could make one for Mega Strength as well. <br /> I think that the many strength related Mega Edges relating to attacks are reason to consider going the other way, but easy enough to do either.<br /> <br /> But what question are you talking about? There are two paths to making super strong attacks. Both are explicitly laid out. <br /> <br /> I think reduced tag would be the way to go for making it cheaper to use. Duration would make the single attack last longer which is a messy interaction with this power. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T10:22:13-07:00","id":1452356,"title":"","content":"Wait, Mateus, are you saying you don't think it's obvious to use Mega-Might to give power Scale for physical attacks? I think that pretty obviously falls under &quot;damaging things using sheer muscle power.&quot; &quot;Things&quot; can also mean people as well as objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T14:01:10-07:00","id":1452371,"title":"","content":"The point is \u201csheer muscle power\u201d. I don\u2019t define a punch as a sheer muscle power, yes it uses muscle power, but it\u2019s a combination of speed, precision and pure muscle, sure a big and strong guy can punch stupidly hard because his powerful muscles can give his hand a tremendous speed in a fraction of a second, it\u2019s how our muscle work, it\u2019s all bout giving potency a Fast output that can be sustained.<br /> But Mega Might don\u2019t necessarily means power, for example, a crane (the mechanical, not the big bird) can lift a few tons but it can\u2019t give the speed it to use the hook as an effective weapon (the demolition ball, is designed to put speed and weight, but a hook don\u2019t). If you think a Mega Might Nova has the power of a crane, the punch will not be that strong because it can\u2019t accelerate the fist fast enough to impact, so no scale in the punch.<br /> <br /> Yes it gets really annoying, I am quite an annoying person... but again, I don\u2019t see a punch a sheer muscle power, while crunching a can in your hands (or a car, or a house, or a skull for that end) is definitely sheer muscle power.<br /> <br /> In the end, this approach balances Mega Might to the other Mega Physical. It was not my idea, by the way, it was a discussion in the discord sometime (like one year) ago, where I was defending MM the opposite I defend today, and after that changed my mind (not by the time of discussion, but later, thinking by myself).<br /> <br /> By the way, I don\u2019t think it\u2019s the kind of thing you must use in the table, I just think it\u2019s a good way to see it and it works fine...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T14:27:15-07:00","id":1452379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1452371#post1452371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is \u201csheer muscle power\u201d. I don\u2019t define a punch as a sheer muscle power, yes it uses muscle power, but it\u2019s a combination of speed, precision and pure muscle, sure a big and strong guy can punch stupidly hard because his powerful muscles can give his hand a tremendous speed in a fraction of a second, it\u2019s how our muscle work, it\u2019s all bout giving potency a Fast output that can be sustained.<br /> But Mega Might don\u2019t necessarily means power, for example, a crane (the mechanical, not the big bird) can lift a few tons but it can\u2019t give the speed it to use the hook as an effective weapon (the demolition ball, is designed to put speed and weight, but a hook don\u2019t). If you think a Mega Might Nova has the power of a crane, the punch will not be that strong because it can\u2019t accelerate the fist fast enough to impact, so no scale in the punch.<br /> <br /> Yes it gets really annoying, I am quite an annoying person... but again, I don\u2019t see a punch a sheer muscle power, while crunching a can in your hands (or a car, or a house, or a skull for that end) is definitely sheer muscle power.<br /> <br /> In the end, this approach balances Mega Might to the other Mega Physical. It was not my idea, by the way, it was a discussion in the discord sometime (like one year) ago, where I was defending MM the opposite I defend today, and after that changed my mind (not by the time of discussion, but later, thinking by myself).<br /> <br /> By the way, I don\u2019t think it\u2019s the kind of thing you must use in the table, I just think it\u2019s a good way to see it and it works fine...</div> </div> </div> </div>Super odd house rule you have. Completely unsupported by the game but do you. <br /> <br /> Might is a stat, not pure muscle. It is effectiveness in using your might. It makes you good at hitting people. Mega-Might has only the faintest relation to ideas of momentum impulse and force soooo you arguments about muscle power really dont have a point. <br /> <br /> Trying to balance individual power purchases in Aberrant is both an excercise in futility but also not really the point of the mechanics. Your proposed change doesnt balance Mega stamina the far weakest of the three. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T15:35:46-07:00","id":1452384,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think it\u2019s futility to balance the powers, they are very diverse and it\u2019s hard to quantify utility, I agree to that, but at same time you have the cost/effect during the session that is a common ground to balance. Physical attributes are mainly used in combat, as well as many of the powers, and the combat scenes are the ones with the highest quantum consuming scenes by far (at least usually).<br /> <br /> While most uses of Mega Attributes are largely passive, granting effects when dealing in certain conditions with no need to activate, none is as unbeatable as Mega Might damage output for 2 reasons:<br /> First it\u2019s free, no activation cost, no Mega Edge to start using, no duration, basically you need Quantum and Mega Might to distribute a stead damage for as long as the combat last.<br /> Second, and most important, it\u2019s one scale above ALL defensive powers, to resist any punch in equal condition a target needs Q+1 I\u2019ve the attacker. Yes you can stake the Soft Armor of armor and quantum field, but not the scale, and it\u2019s a big advantage.<br /> <br /> In other words, it balance much better than you may expect at first look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T16:12:03-07:00","id":1452388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1449664-aberrant-understanding-scale-through-specific-examples?p=1452384#post1452384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think it\u2019s futility to balance the powers, they are very diverse and it\u2019s hard to quantify utility, I agree to that, but at same time you have the cost/effect during the session that is a common ground to balance. Physical attributes are mainly used in combat, as well as many of the powers, and the combat scenes are the ones with the highest quantum consuming scenes by far (at least usually).<br /> <br /> While most uses of Mega Attributes are largely passive, granting effects when dealing in certain conditions with no need to activate, none is as unbeatable as Mega Might damage output for 2 reasons:<br /> First it\u2019s free, no activation cost, no Mega Edge to start using, no duration, basically you need Quantum and Mega Might to distribute a stead damage for as long as the combat last.<br /> Second, and most important, it\u2019s one scale above ALL defensive powers, to resist any punch in equal condition a target needs Q+1 I\u2019ve the attacker. Yes you can stake the Soft Armor of armor and quantum field, but not the scale, and it\u2019s a big advantage.<br /> <br /> In other words, it balance much better than you may expect at first look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that physical attributes are mainly used in combat. They are only the most used in combat. <br /> <br /> See but mega might 1-2 is easily matched by household weapons, it just makes you punching viable. A pistol or a rifle puts baselines on a Power scale of 2-3. <br /> <br /> I dont think its a big advantage. You will at most ever get +4 sucesses from mismatched scale on meaningful opposition. Defense is layered much more easily than offense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10020-manifoldpersona","name":"Manifoldpersona","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T16:14:59-07:00","id":1452389,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the book mentions that the mega attributes are only partially physical and that part of them is the nova manipulating quantum forces unconsciously so that they can function that's why nova's can pick up objects which should fall apart from their own weight or punch as hard as they do without abiding by the normal laws of physics like baselines have to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T05:24:20-07:00","id":1452451,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the crane example doesn't really hold weight when novas are involved. The book explicitly states Mega-Might doesn't 100% follow the rules of physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:21:11-07:00","id":1452459,"title":"","content":"Well, I don\u2019t really care much about the laws of physics when dealing with Novas, but I do care about how the powers work in game and how they may be balanced or not when the players have to deal with a lack of resources while others just don\u2019t use their quantum at all, or the fact one of them is one scale above all the time.<br /> <br /> The idea of the crane was more about example of how power (the energy output measure) works, not comparing a Nova to a crane.<br /> <br /> But ok, I will give another example this time on the \u201cnot following physics rules\u201d.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s describe Mega Might as touch range telekinesis, it\u2019s not really it, as there is still the need to grab, but it work pretty similar.<br /> <br /> The nova touch the target and move it using only his telekinetic power that he basically can\u2019t project further than touch, but once touching he can lift a huge amount of material with no physical effort.<br /> <br /> Usually, characters that can lift objects with telekinesis are not automatically capable of using it as a weapon, so it\u2019s hard to them to accelerate it fast enough to cause damage, you need a tag that allows you to do so, the attack tag. You can also question the capacity of destroying the object using telekinesis, that is basically what a Mega Might user can do by crushing it with his hands, not really causing impact but smashing by continuous pressure.<br /> <br /> Now back to the touch telekinesis, you can say when the nova moves his fist and touch the target he immediately discharge a huge telekinetic force over the target, that would be the attack, it can be part of Mega Might Mega Attribute, but it\u2019s a tag to other kinds of telekinesis, so it should be a tag (or Mega Edge, or independent power) to Mega Might too.<br /> <br /> You can always say a nova don\u2019t follow the physics laws, and so, a Mega Speed character should be able to do a lot of damage easily just because he is as fast as a bullet and the size of a person, even an automatic sonic boom could be a side effect of running at Speed scale 6+, but no one question it would be unbalanced. It\u2019s a paradigm, you think mega might should cause damage, so you don\u2019t question it, I think it\u2019s about constant pressure and lifting, and so high impact is not a immediate effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:42:48-07:00","id":1452462,"title":"","content":"The thing is, the fact they DON'T follow the laws of physics is what keeps speedsters from automatically doing a lot of damage or causing sonic booms without buying the powers to model them.<br /> <br /> The other thing is all of the mega-edges dealing with mega-might do things like increasing power Scale vs. inanimate objects only. (If mega-might doesn't apply to people, then why make the distinction?) Or else they do things like allowing you to attack everyone within Close range. You'd think if you couldn't use mega-might in normal close attacks, they'd have a mega-edge to do that since they have ones to let you attack an area. Why an area but not a single target?<br /> <br /> You can run things how you want, but I'm 99% certain the authors intended mega-might to add to physical attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T09:44:53-07:00","id":1452494,"title":"","content":"I can get where your coming in regards to having to spend quantum of not to achieve certain effects. But players have to consider these things when making their characters and how they want them to work, what theme if any are they using, what powers do they want, what do they think would be cool.<br /> <br /> when you start looking too deeply the physics or lack of physics and how you think powers should manifest or work a lot of problems start coming up.<br /> <br /> Like Florin said you can run the game however you want if that's what it takes for you and the players to have fun. I'm sure the developers tried to take everything into consideration when trying to make everything balanced.<br /> <br /> If you think a certain power should have certain effects I'm certain tags could be used to make it so. Like mega speed causing sonic booms if high enough and causing damage. I'm not sure about 2e but in 1e characters did cause sonic booms if moving fast enough, they were immune to the effect but still caused it and I think you could buy an enhancement that allowed you not to cause them. I'm sure something similar could be done in 2e maybe some version of the innocuous power tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T10:22:30-07:00","id":1452499,"title":"","content":"Sonic booms in 2e can either be a q. attack, or I would adapt the Thunderclap mega-edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T10:36:54-07:00","id":1452500,"title":"","content":"In TC you basically pay by effect when building your powers, so Mega Speed has no side effects, unless you buy them as a Mega Edge, Power or Technique.<br /> <br /> You could improvise a sonic boom, even not having the power using a Power Stunt or Maxing Out (the first is easier, but you need the second to train the power. Those 2 options are one of the best thing in TC Aberrant and they are how I put most of the \u201conce in a life time\u201d powers many super heroes have and that once when the character did \u201cthat amazing feat that never repeated again\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}